  {
   "text": "How does a substitute win a final in under nineteen minutes?",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.44
  },
  {
   "text": "Spain led, then England equalised in the seventy-third minute.",
   "start": 3.96,
   "end": 7.1
  },
  {
   "text": "Cole Palmer, a substitute, scored two minutes after coming on.",
   "start": 7.66,
   "end": 11.04
  },
  {
   "text": "Spain's answer: substitute Mikel Oyarzabal, on in the sixty-seventh minute.",
   "start": 11.54,
   "end": 16.56
  },
  {
   "text": "Cucurella passed along the ground, and Oyarzabal scored in the eighty-sixth.",
   "start": 16.56,
   "end": 21.067
  },
  {
   "text": "StatsBomb's model rated the chance at point two eight expected goals.",
   "start": 21.067,
   "end": 25.26
  },
  {
   "text": "Eighteen minutes after coming on.",
   "start": 25.26,
   "end": 27.82
  },
  {
   "text": "Two of the three goals in that final came from substitutes.",
   "start": 28.37,
   "end": 30.98
  },
  {
   "text": "Full breakdown on our channel.",
   "start": 31.82,
   "end": 33.12
